# Workflow

## Plan strong, execute small

- The parent agent (the strongest model in the session) owns planning: reads `docs/bellhopper-plan.md` and `TODO.md`, breaks a phase into tasks small enough to describe in one paragraph, and verifies results.
- Implementation and test writing are **always** delegated to smaller models. Default channel is the headless CLI: `scripts/delegate.sh <role> <model> "<brief>"`. Roles are `.cursor/agents/*.md`. Give each a self-contained brief: task, plan sections to read, files in scope, acceptance criteria. Run independent tasks in parallel (background shell jobs).
- Pick the model by complexity, not by habit:
  - `composer-2.5` or `grok-4.7-medium` — mechanical, well-specified: routes, schemas, wrappers, UI components, tests.
  - `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` — multi-file logic with edge cases: executors, context layer, event processor.
  - `claude-opus-5-5-medium` — core guarantees: approvals, idempotency, recovery, state machine.
- The parent may make small fixes itself (a few lines, a config value, a doc edit). Anything larger goes back to a delegate.
- If a delegate reports a conflict with the plan, resolve it with the user before continuing; do not let it guess.
- IDE Task-tool subagents (same names) are the fallback when the CLI is unavailable.

## Review panel — milestone gates only

The panel takes 1–8 minutes per run depending on model; it is **not** run on every PR during the demo build.

- **Run it** at these gates, on the branch that completes the gate (or on `main` with `BASE=<last-gate-tag>`):
  - end of Phase 2 (core engine: approvals, idempotency, recovery) — security + correctness mandatory
  - end of Phase 3 (harness, limits, trace)
  - end of Phase 6 (API, auth, UI) — security mandatory
  - end of Phase 7 (MCP) — security mandatory
  - any PR the user explicitly asks to review
- **Skip it** for everything else (mocks, schema, seeds, docs, config, UI polish). Say "panel: skipped (not a gate)" in the PR body.
- Command: `scripts/review-panel.sh "<what the gate delivers>" [base]`. Fix BLOCKERs; MAJORs fixed or deferred to `TODO.md` with a reason; MINORs optional. Re-run only the reviewer(s) that raised a blocker: `scripts/delegate.sh <review-role> <model> "<brief>" --readonly`.
- Record each gate review in `LOGS.md` (verdicts, blockers fixed, deferred).

## Stacked PRs per phase

- Each phase has an integration branch `feat/phase-<n>-<name>` off `main`.
- Parallel tasks run as delegates in isolated worktrees: `scripts/delegate.sh implementer <model> "<brief>" --worktree=p<n>-<task>`. Each gets its own branch off the phase branch. Keep tasks on disjoint paths; shared surfaces (root `package.json`, lockfile, `@bellhop/shared` API) are settled in the phase's first wave before anything depends on them.
- The parent verifies each worktree (lint, typecheck, test), commits there, pushes, and opens a PR **into the phase branch**; merge with rebase. Remove the worktree after merge (`git worktree remove`).
- When the phase exit criteria pass on the integration branch, one PR brings it into `main`. Gate phases run the review panel on that PR only.

## Git — PRs only

- **Nothing reaches `main` except via a pull request.** Never commit, push, or merge locally into `main`. Branch per task: `feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `chore/`, `test/`. Guards: the `pre-push` hook blocks pushes to `main`; `.cursor/cli.json` denies `git push/commit/merge` and `gh` to CLI delegates entirely (parent owns git). GitHub branch protection needs a paid plan for private repos; the rule holds regardless.
- Conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`), enforced by commitlint. Small, meaningful commits.
- Merge with `gh pr merge --rebase --delete-branch` to keep the linear history of small commits.

## Docs discipline (from the plan)

- New bug found → `BUGS.md` entry (what broke, why, fix, regression test name) **at the moment it happens**.
- Decision made → one line in `LOGS.md` under today's date.
- Task done or discovered → update `TODO.md`.
- `EVALS.md` is generated by the test reporter; never hand-edit.
- `docs/internal/` is private reference material; never read it into a commit, never cite it in committed docs.
